<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2599" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ănĭcŭla</span></b>  (sync.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ănĭcla</span></b> ,
		Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. στεφ</span>. 6, 149),
		ae, f.
		dim.
		anus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				little old woman</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">neque illi benivolens extra unam aniculam
					quisquam aderat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Phorm. 1, 2, 48</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">importunitatem spectate aniculae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					And. 1, 4, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">haec ne aniculae quidem existimant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Div. 2, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ista sunt tota commenticia, vix digna
					lucubratione anicularum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. N.
					D. 1, 34</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">1, 20</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Fl.
			36</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 77 al.</span></i></div>
